From 762e06a4982196a017635780907437f04759ccf5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rigaz29 <ryanbagas27@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:24:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fs: add susfs v2.3.0 sus_mount, stage 1 for 3.10

Port the mount hiding from the 4.4 non-GKI susfs patch to 3.10:
mounts made or cloned by su domain processes get fake mnt_ids from
DEFAULT_KSU_MNT_ID on, and /proc/mounts, mountinfo and mountstats skip
them for non-su processes while the hide static key is enabled.

3.10 adaptations:
- mnt_id allocator: 3.10 has no ida_simple_get(); use the ida_pre_get +
  ida_get_new_above dance and never bump mnt_id_start, so normal mount
  ids stay in the low range.
- The alloc_vfsmnt copies keep 3.10's mnt_fsnotify_marks init and use
  plain kstrdup (kstrdup_const is 3.13+).
- __lookup_mnt iterates a list_head in 3.10 (hlist in 4.4); the sus
  mount skip checks p->mnt_id < DEFAULT_KSU_MNT_ID on the list walk.
- CL_COPY_MNT_NS is added in dup_mnt_ns() (copy_mnt_ns() in 4.4).
- susfs_is_current_ksu_domain() maps to KernelSU backslashxx's
  is_ksu_domain() SID check; susfs_is_current_proc_umounted() maps to
  the fork's TIF_KSU_UNMOUNTABLE flag (61/29), keeping
  include/linux/susfs_def.h in sync with app_profile.h.
- Set VFSMOUNT_MNT_FLAGS_KSU_UNSHARED_MNT right after the unshare
  alloc in clone_mnt so mnt_free_id() cannot ida_remove() the borrowed
  mnt_id on error paths (sdcardfs has clone_mnt_data, so the path is
  reachable here). Upstream 4.4 sets the flag only after the mnt_flags
  copy, leaving the window open.
- DEFINE_STATIC_KEY_TRUE(susfs_is_sdcard_android_data_not_decrypted)
  is hoisted out of the sus_path guard: namespace.c references it from
  the sus_mount hooks and sus_path is not built yet.
---
